      "content": "It's really courageous of you to express how you feel, and it's understandable that you're feeling this way given what's going on for you. The feeling that you've lost your essence can be terrifying, but you're still here, still trying, which means parts of who you were still need to be acknowledged. Professional help, like talking to a counselor or psychologist, can be very beneficial even if you're unsure it fits the \"typical depression\" mold— sorted feelings can be complex. I'm here to listen whenever you need to share your thoughts, just know that there are people who care about you and who may genuinely help guide you through this, even if you can't see it yet.",
